# SABOTAGE: rule 4 of the co-adoption table — the realtime PubSub (ADR-012 §6.3 chat / ADR-016 §4
# notifications). The counterpart signal is short-circuited to `[true]`, so no app can be reported
# as mounting a chat/notifications surface on a bus it does not run: both macros' @docs say the
# realtime path "needs a running Phoenix.PubSub", the chat room's connected mount subscribes and
# tracks presence on it, and the framework's own default is a VERTICAL's name (`Driftwood.PubSub`).
# A mount that names no `:pubsub` label therefore broadcasts on the wrong bus — or crashes the room
# on connect — with nothing red in the build.
# HONEST DISCLOSURE: the scan still computes the signal (label, supervised children, name match), so
# the green real-tree proof stays green; the rule-4 RED test plus the name-mismatch and missing-roster
# anti-tautology assertions flip. Rules 1-3 and every other check are untouched.
# RE-ANCHORED (`--root`): the hunk's TRAILING context used to be `app_dirs/1`'s comment, which the
# `--root` work rewrote (the `rule_signal/2` clauses above it are untouched). Only the context and
# line numbers move: the removed and added lines, the defect and the MUST_FAIL target are
# byte-identical to the original. The hunk was regenerated with `diff -u` rather than re-typed, so
# its workspace-context bytes (including the blank context line) are the file's own.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/verify_fleet_wire_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED (rule 4): a chat mount with no supervision tree in the app is a violation
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex b/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/mix/tasks/samen.verify.fleet_wire.ex
